 "comments": "This <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Mule Coin</span> was issued in 2008 by the Stuttgart Mint. It was supposed to have the &quot;New&quot; Europe Map on the reverse. The Stuttgart Mint (F) accidentally issued 600,000 of them with the &quot;Old&quot; Europe Map on the reverse. They realised their error and issued their remaining allocation, 9,000,000, with the correct reverse. The coin has got a separate KM# (KM# A261) from the correctly issued coin (KM# 261)<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/627f573685b00.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/627f573685b00.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a>",
